= render 'shared/breakthrough_page', page_title: 'Hodgical Test Mode', current_page: 'Hodgical Test Mode', page_subtitle: 'Easy debugging of pixel and model issues on the Baldrick8', document_title: 'Hodgical Test Mode - Baldrick8 Debugging Feature', meta: ['Baldrick8 feature', 'Per-model RGB offset', 'Quick debugging'] do
  p.lead The Hodgical Test is a mode on the Baldrick8 which allows for easy debugging of pixel and model issues.

  .prose
    .callout.info
      span.ic
        svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2"
          circle cx="12" cy="12" r="10"
          path d="M12 16v-4M12 8h.01"
      div
        span.lbl How it works
        p.bd The Hodgical Test runs the RGB cycle on each model on a port but each subsequent model starts with the subsequent colour.

    h2
      span.hk
        span.bar
        span.annot Demo
      | Visual example

    figure.figure
      .fimg
        = image_tag 'hodgical-test-mode.gif', alt: 'Hodgical Test Mode animation'
      figcaption Hodgical Test Mode in action — showing the RGB cycle pattern across models on a port.

    h2
      span.hk
        span.bar
        span.annot Pattern
      | How it works

    p You can see here these three stars on the same port:

    .spec-grid
      .spec.star-card
        span.ic
          span.dot.red
        h4 Star 1
        p
          | Starts with
          strong  RED
          | , then goes
          strong  GREEN
          |  then goes
          strong  BLUE
      .spec.star-card
        span.ic
          span.dot.green
        h4 Star 2
        p
          | Starts with
          strong  GREEN
          | , then goes
          strong  BLUE
          |  then goes
          strong  RED
      .spec.star-card
        span.ic
          span.dot.blue
        h4 Star 3
        p
          | Starts with
          strong  BLUE
          | , then goes
          strong  RED
          |  then goes
          strong  GREEN

    .callout.info
      span.ic
        svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2"
          circle cx="12" cy="12" r="10"
          path d="M12 16v-4M12 8h.01"
      div
        span.lbl And if you had a fourth…
        p.bd If we had a star four that would go RED then GREEN then BLUE.

    h2
      span.hk
        span.bar
        span.annot Why
      | Why Hodgical Mode

    p This allows us to quickly:

    .spec-grid
      .spec
        span.ic
          svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.9"
            path d="M12 9v4M12 17h.01M10.29 3.86L1.82 18a2 2 0 0 0 1.71 3h16.94a2 2 0 0 0 1.71-3L13.71 3.86a2 2 0 0 0-3.42 0z"
        h4 Debug pixel issues
        p Check if pixels are failing on any specific colour value.
      .spec
        span.ic
          svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.9"
            path d="M9 12l2 2 4-4"
            circle cx="12" cy="12" r="10"
        h4 Verify model setup
        p Confirm the models are set up correctly — is half of your snowflake the wrong colour?
      .spec
        span.ic
          svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.9"
            path d="M13 2 4 14h7l-1 8 9-12h-7z"
        h4 Quick demo
        p Put something up on the house when someone comes over and wants to see it working.

    .callout.warn
      span.ic
        svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2"
          path d="M10.3 3.9 1.8 18a2 2 0 0 0 1.7 3h17a2 2 0 0 0 1.7-3L13.7 3.9a2 2 0 0 0-3.4 0z"
      div
        span.lbl No, I mean why did you call it Hodgical
        p.bd Because it was an idea from Dom Hodgson (although obviously Pete did all the work) and so obvious his ego wouldn't let it be named something NORMAL.

    h2
      span.hk
        span.bar
        span.annot RGB vs wash
      | Why RGB, why not a colour wash?

    p A colour wash starting at different times on props can be overwhelming with colour and takes longer to debug issues (it also doesn't look as good as you might think).

    .spec-grid
      .spec
        span.ic
          svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.9"
            path d="M18 6L6 18M6 6l12 12"
        h4 Colour wash problems
        p Overwhelming with colour, takes longer to debug and doesn't look as good as expected.
      .spec
        span.ic
          svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.9"
            path d="M9 12l2 2 4-4"
            circle cx="12" cy="12" r="10"
        h4 RGB cycle benefits
        p Clear colour separation, easy to identify issues, professional appearance and quick debugging.

    h2
      span.hk
        span.bar
        span.annot Use cases
      | Practical applications

    ul
      li
        strong During setup
        |  — verify all pixels are working, check colour order is correct, identify dead or stuck pixels and test power distribution.
      li
        strong During shows
        |  — quick visual check of system health, demonstrate the system to visitors, identify issues during operation.

    h2
      span.hk
        span.bar
        span.annot Keep reading
      | Related breakthroughs

    .next-grid
      = link_to breakthroughs_cunningfx_path, class: 'next-card' do
        .top
          span.kind Breakthrough
          span.go →
        h4 CunningFX
        p Built-in effects when you're past the debugging stage.
      = link_to board_path('baldrick8'), class: 'next-card' do
        .top
          span.kind Docs
          span.go →
        h4 Baldrick8
        p The board Hodgical Test Mode lives on.
      = link_to board_page_path('baldrick8', 'manual'), class: 'next-card' do
        .top
          span.kind Manual
          span.go →
        h4 Baldrick8 manual
        p Setup, wiring and web interface walkthrough.
      = link_to breakthroughs_path, class: 'next-card' do
        .top
          span.kind Index
          span.go →
        h4 All breakthroughs
        p Explore everything that makes Baldrick boards a bit special.

section.cta
  .wrap
    h2 Debug faster, show sooner
    p Hodgical Test Mode is built into the Baldrick8 — one less thing to wire up from scratch.
    .cta-btns
      = link_to board_path('baldrick8'), class: 'btn btn-bone' do
        | Meet the Baldrick8
        span.ar →
      = link_to where_to_buy_baldrick_boards_path, class: 'btn btn-clear' do
        | Where to buy
